Package: DspikeIn
Type: Package
Title: Estimating absolute abundance from microbial spike-in controls
Version: 0.99.0
Authors@R: 
    person(given = "Mitra", family = "Ghotbi", 
           role = c("aut", "cre"), 
           email = "mitra.ghotbi@gmail.com",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-9185-9993"))
Description: Provides tools for absolute microbial quantification using both 
    'phyloseq' and 'TreeSummarizedExperiment' (TSE) data structures. Supports 
    single spike-in taxa or synthetic communities with flexible spike-in volumes 
    and copy numbers. Implements a complete workflow including spike-in validation, 
    data preprocessing, scaling factor estimation, conversion to absolute abundances, 
    bias correction, normalization, and downstream analyses. Offers visualization 
    and interactive plots via 'ggplot2' and 'ggtree'. Enables analysis with 
    'DESeq2', 'edgeR', and other methods. Includes vignette tutorials, case 
    studies, and comprehensive documentation.
